<com:TContent ID="body">
<h1>TConditional Samples</h1>

<table class="sampletable">

<tr><td class="samplenote">
A condition that holds, so the <tt>TrueTemplate</tt> renders. The running version is
compared against 4.0.0, without naming the current version anywhere:
</td><td class="sampleaction">
<com:TConditional Condition="version_compare(Prado::getVersion(), '4.0.0', '>=')">
<prop:TrueTemplate>
  <com:TLabel Text="This application runs PRADO 4.0.0 or later." />
</prop:TrueTemplate>
<prop:FalseTemplate>
  <com:TLabel Text="This application runs a PRADO release older than 4.0.0." />
</prop:FalseTemplate>
</com:TConditional>
</td></tr>

<tr><td class="samplenote">
The same control with a condition that fails, so the <tt>FalseTemplate</tt> renders
instead. The running version is reported by <tt>Prado::getVersion()</tt>:
</td><td class="sampleaction">
<com:TConditional Condition="version_compare(Prado::getVersion(), '99.0.0', '>=')">
<prop:TrueTemplate>
  <com:TLabel Text="This application runs PRADO 99.0.0 or later." />
</prop:TrueTemplate>
<prop:FalseTemplate>
  <com:TLabel Text="<%= 'This application runs PRADO ' . Prado::getVersion() . ', which is older than 99.0.0.' %>" />
</prop:FalseTemplate>
</com:TConditional>
</td></tr>

<tr><td class="samplenote">
A control with no <tt>FalseTemplate</tt>. When the condition fails, the control renders
nothing at all:
</td><td class="sampleaction">
<com:TConditional Condition="false">
<prop:TrueTemplate>
  <com:TLabel Text="You will not see this." />
</prop:TrueTemplate>
</com:TConditional>
(nothing renders above this line)
</td></tr>

</table>

</com:TContent>
